Possibly you have a half duplex connection and you have it set for full
duplex. Switch it and you'll be happy.

Some of the early NIC hardware did not properly automatically decide what it
was connected to such as half or full duplex or 10 or 100 MBPS. Some reasons
for this is that 10 MBPS hubs and switches did not do the negotiation thing
at all and left the connecting unit confused or it would connect up and then
go through a re-negotiation phase every once in a while.

Remember, older network hard never did any negotiation for connection or
speed and can leave newer hardware confused, thus you have to manually set
the connection up to work reliably.

rtt


