On the disk drives, the "L" generally meant "low-profile" or "lower-cost".  
The "N" doesn't really have a meaning -- it's just a different variant of a 
1GB drive.

The -AA and -AS are the vendors of the drive.  Look at the labels to find 
out which is which.

The letters after the BA356-?? mean a variety of things.  Give an example 
of what you're looking for.
