Alex wrote:
> 
>   To: Comp.Sys.Dec
> I need to transfer a tape image created in unix over to a microvax II running
> vms 5.5. My current idea is to hook the vax up to my current network of linux
> machines and install decnet on both.  Is this the best way to do this? I have
> no other dec hardware.
> 
> Also, what program will I need to write the image to tape when it has been sent
> to the machine?

TCP/IP should do it.

1. dd the tape to disk on the UN*X system. If possible, determine the
blocksize of the tape image. VMS will default to 512 if you can't
determine it.

2. FTP the tape image to VMS as binary

3. Use this sequence to write the tape:

$ MOUNT/FOREIGN tape_drive:/BLOCKSIZE=block_size_previously_determined
$ COPY tape_image_file tape_drive:
$ DISMOUNT tape_drive:

A disk/tape device on VMS MOUNTed /FOREIGN is the (rough) equivalent of
a UN*X-land "raw" device.

Good luck.

