Look for these logical names:

$ SH LOG UCX*
(Old-style DEC Ultrix Connection)

$ SH LOG TCPIP*
(TCP/IP Services for OpenVMS, successor to UCX)

$ SH LOG MULTINET*
(Process Software Multinet, previously from TGV or Cisco)

$ SH LOG TCPWARE*
(Process Software TCPware)

There is also the remote possibibility that either Wollongong's TCP/IP
or CMU/IP may be present. Dunno what the indicators are.

