I'm not sure that a BIOS update would allow full support of the 10GB drive.
Unfortunately, the Phoenix BIOSes used in the bone white DEC boxes is a little
bit quirky.  You might check and double-check the jumper settings again before
trying to flash one more time.  The message you cite indicates a failure to
flash either because writing to flash was jumper-disabled or something was not
100% right with the flash module itself.

I suggest a 3rd party card with its own hard disk BIOS, which effectively
replaces the motherboard BIOS.

If you want to pump up the speed of the FX-2, I have AMD processors, DEC voltage
regulators and cooling fans to get the system to 400MHz.  Not to expensive these
days.  But get the hard disk right before putting more money into the system.

... Ben Myers

