See the link below for the lead layout at the supply reel end, all the 
TKXX and TZXX drives look the same. The leader attaches to the take-up 
reel on a hook thru a slot in the centre of the reel, then follows the 
tape path,round all rollers, and in front of the head, then forward to 
the supply reel, where it hooks over the load arm, and the end toes 
forward into the cartridge, where it catches the tape-end when the 
cartridge is inserted, and the flap is opened. remember, the tape end 
hook should be clearly visible in the centre of the opening, when you 
open the flap to check it, by pressing the unlock button in the hinge.
A more likely cause of read errs is dirty head or tape. You can remove 
the cover from over the head then raise the head against the springs, 
and clean with a soft cloth and tape cleaning fluid. Of course, if the 
tape loads ok, there is nothing wrong with the leader, and head/tape 
dirty is the likely cause.

