healyzh@aracnet.com wrote:
> 
> Zoong Pham <dpham@mercy_dot_com.au> wrote:
> > How can I "plagiarize the tape" ?
> 
> VMSTPC is your friend.

As is dd on UN*X.

In VMS land, as long as the tape blocksize is 32767 or less, you can
MOUNT/FOREIGN both the source and target drives and COPY from one to the
other. A final SET MAGTAPE/END will write the second tape mark
signalling end of tape.

If you don't have two tape drives on your VMS system, you can COPY the
individual "datasets" to disk, and COPY them out to the target tape in
the correct order. There's freeware for that, I'm sure, or you can roll
your own. Again, a final SET MAGTAPE/END will write the second tape mark
signalling end of tape.

