DECdirect Catalogue:
"The VAX 11/730 and 11/25 memory options support a maximum memory
configuration of 3 and 5 megabytes." and goes on to describe MS730 add-on
memory (1MB at $A1,708). 1 MB card size times the number of memory slots
give the memory limitation above.

VAX Hardware Handbook, Basic Memory Operations:
"The physical address space contained in the memory controller is devided
into two areas: physical memory addresses and I/O addresses. A physical
address is 24 bits, allowing a total address space of 16 MB. Figure 4-2
illustrates the combined areas."
 000000 - EFFFFF Memory space 15 MB
 F00000 - FFFFFF I/O space 1 MB

There is more info in the handbook show UNIBUS (18-bits) to memory (24-bits)
translation.

Hope that helps.




