reconnected or powered up, with the exception of the RA92 drives.  Three of
those started and passed self test, one failed to start.

I've got a list of board numbers, but I'm not sure what all of them are.  I
started out on AlphaServer 2100s and never dealt with VAXen much.  Some of
the memory may have been removed at some point (leased?), but I'm not sure.
I got this beast for free, not counting the doctor's bill for a sprained
wrist from carrying around RA92's.  I was hoping to restore it, but
especially considering the 3-phase power requirement I'm not sure I'll ever
do it.

The system is in California, on the central coast.  If you want it, you can
either pick it up yourself or arrange transportation.  I'm willing to give
it away free to another DEC enthusiast, but if you're after it for
commercial value (parts or scrap) I'd be happy to work something out to help
make up for my storage expenses.  And I WILL NOT part it out and be left
with a stripped chassis - you get the whole thing out of my garage, or no
deal.  =]

Yeah, 10 years from now I'll probably regret getting rid of it, like I
regret giving away my Commodore PETs, but I'm looking at moving again in the
near future and with the possible exception of my car, this is the most
massive posession I own.  I don't look forward to moving it yet again.

